---
id: org.dxos.plugin.review
name: ReviewPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

ReviewPlugin is the **review layer** over ECHO objects (primarily Markdown documents) — the merge of
the former comments and versioning plugins into one surface. It contributes three anchored,
attributed review mechanisms and the surfaces that operate them:

- **Comment threads** — anchored discussions, with an optional per-thread AI agent that answers and
  may propose document edits.
- **Suggestions** — Google-Docs-style proposed changes authored on per-user `kind:'suggestion'`
  branches, rendered inline (tracked changes / multi-author overlay) and as reviewable change-block
  cards (accept/reject), with per-author colours and per-author visibility toggles.
- **Version history** — named checkpoints, draft branches, time travel, compare/merge, and the
  git-graph Timeline companion.

The editor integration is inverted: `@dxos/plugin-markdown` owns neutral sockets
(`EditorBindingHook`, `ExtensionProvider`, `ViewModeExtension`) and this plugin contributes the
behaviour — the version-aware editor binding, the comment-sync extension, and the "Suggesting" view
mode. It depends on no other plugin: message/thread UI comes from `@dxos/react-ui-thread`,
review/diff primitives from `@dxos/ui-editor`, branch machinery from `@dxos/versioning`, and the
`Thread`/`Message`/`AnchoredTo` schema from `@dxos/types`.

Companion documents: [DESIGN.md](./DESIGN.md) (three-layer spec, invariants I-1..I-9 each naming its
enforcing test, known risks) and [TEST-PLAN.md](./TEST-PLAN.md) (test tiers, shared scenarios, F1–F6
walkthrough scripts).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0`          |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`     |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`        |

## External types & capabilities

The review layer composes primitives owned elsewhere; the plugin binds to them rather than
redefining them:

- `Thread`, `Message`, `AnchoredTo` (`@dxos/types`) — the anchored-annotation schema. `AnchoredTo`
  carries an optional `branch` tag scoping an annotation to a review branch (undefined = main).
- `Branch`, `Version`, `History` (`@dxos/versioning`) — branches (core CRDT branches keyed in the
  database registry; a per-user suggestion branch is `kind:'suggestion'` keyed by author `creator`
  DID), checkpoints, fork anchors, `contentAt` snapshots. Find-or-create of the suggestion branch is
  identity-stable and serialized per (doc, creator); a stale branch is reconciled by folding main IN
  (`db.syncBranch`, CRDT merge), never by re-forking.
- `SuggestionSource`, `trackChanges`, `suggestions({ sources, base })`, `suggestionsOverlay`,
  `changeBarGutter`, `diffHunks`/`groupHunks`/`pairMarkupHunks`/`rebaseHunks`, `cherryPickHunk`/
  `revertHunk`, `automerge` (`@dxos/ui-editor`) — the inline diff/overlay/sync primitives. Word-level
  hunks are minimized (an insert adjacent to identical text never strikes it), markdown delimiter
  pairs coalesce into one atomic hunk, and accept/reject merge every hunk a range spans.
- `MarkdownCapabilities.EditorBindingHook` / `ExtensionProvider` / `ViewModeExtension`
  (`@dxos/plugin-markdown`) — the sockets this plugin contributes to.
- `CollaborationOperation.AcceptChange` / `RejectChange` / `AcceptProposal` (`@dxos/app-toolkit`) —
  the durable cherry-pick/revert ops every review surface routes accept/reject through.
- `ViewState` (`@dxos/react-ui-attention`) — the per-session, per-object state backend for the
  `viewAspect` (version selection, review mode, current change, hidden authors) and the comments
  companion view state.

## Types

```mdl
type ReviewMode
  literals: editing | suggesting | viewing
  desc: Per-user editing posture for a document (Google-Docs-style). Session-local, never replicated.
```

```mdl
type VersionSelection
  desc: |
    Which version of an object the local user is viewing: the current tip, a branch (editable tip),
    a branch's fork point (read-only parent snapshot), or a checkpoint. Session-local.
  literals: current | branch(branchId) | fork(branchId) | checkpoint(versionId)
```

```mdl
type VersioningView
  desc: |
    Per-object version view state, stored in the ViewState `viewAspect` (in-memory, per session).
    Missing fields fall back to defaults (selection=current, view=branch, mode=editing).
  fields:
    selection?: VersionSelection
    view?: String                 # base | diff | branch — which side of a selected branch shows
    mode?: ReviewMode
    suggestion?: { author: String, from: Number, to: Number }  # the current change, shared by editor + companion
    hiddenAuthors?: String[]      # authors whose suggestions this user has hidden (view filter only)
```

```mdl
type ReviewRenderConfig
  desc: |
    What the editor renders for a review mode: `defaultReviewRenderPolicy` gives GDocs parity —
    editing/suggesting show suggestions+comments and are editable; viewing is read-only, comments only.
    Override by contributing ReviewRenderPolicy earlier in plugin order.
  fields:
    showSuggestions: Boolean
    showComments: Boolean
    editable: Boolean
```

```mdl
type ViewModeSelection
  desc: |
    One dropdown gesture: a built-in editor view mode, or a contributed review mode. The pure
    `applyViewModeSelection` writes BOTH halves of the (review mode, view mode) pair atomically, so a
    contradictory pair (e.g. a stale readonly view mode surviving into Suggesting) cannot be stored
    (invariant I-9).
  literals: builtin(viewMode) | contributed(reviewMode)
```

```mdl
type BindingDescriptor
  desc: |
    Output of the pure `deriveBinding(inputs)` lifecycle derivation (invariant I-8): which document
    backs the editor (main, own suggestion branch, selected branch, or a detached snapshot), keyed
    how, rendered how. All ambient postures share ONE editor key — entering/leaving Suggesting swaps
    the automerge source through a live compartment, never remounting the editor (DESIGN §3.3), so
    caret/focus/scroll survive every mode switch.
  fields:
    subject: String               # document | own-branch | branch | snapshot
    editorKey: String
    effectiveViewMode?: String    # readonly overrides the caller's view mode
    loading: Boolean
    ambient: Boolean
    ambientSuggesting: Boolean
```

```mdl
type ResolvedSuggestionBranch
  desc: |
    A resolved `kind:'suggestion'` branch: its author (identity DID), current content read live from
    the bound branch doc, and the parent text at the branch's fork anchor (`base`) — proposals are
    diffed against the revision they were written on and rebased into the viewing document's
    coordinates, never raw against a moving document (invariant I-3).
  fields:
    author: String
    content: String
    base?: String
    hue?: String
```

```mdl
type SuggestionGroup
  desc: |
    One reviewable suggestion card: a grouped DiffHunk from a single author, anchored in the base
    (main) text, tinted with the author's colour. Changes already present in the document are
    filtered by content match (invariant I-4); markdown delimiter pairs arrive pre-coalesced.
  extends: DiffHunk
  fields:
    author: String
    colour: String
```

```mdl
type AgentMode
  literals: auto | mention
  desc: Per-thread agent firing policy.
```

```mdl
type AgentConfig
  desc: |
    Per-thread agent configuration. Defined in @dxos/types and stored as an optional field on
    Thread.Thread (`agent?`). Absent or disabled means no AI involvement.
  fields:
    enabled: Boolean
    mode: AgentMode
```

```mdl
type AgentIdentity
  desc: |
    Effect/Capability identity of the comment-thread agent, resolved at runtime (not stored on
    threads). The default reads from plugin Settings; tests/stories provide static values. Sole
    source of the agent's display name and @mention token. NOTE: distinct from @dxos/compute's
    `AgentIdentity` service (the suggestion-author DID).
  fields:
    name: String
    identityDid?: String
    avatar?: String
```

```mdl
type CommentsState
  desc: In-memory comment UI state (atom). Keyed by subject/object URI.
  fields:
    toolbar: Map<String, Boolean>     # per-object: does the selection overlap a comment?
    drafts: Map<String, AnchoredTo[]> # staged (unsent) threads per subject
    current?: String                  # currently-selected thread URI
```

## Services

```mdl
service EditorBindingHook
  desc: |
    Implements MarkdownCapabilities.EditorBindingHook (`useMarkdownEditorBinding`): the version-aware
    editor binding. Derives the bound subject through the pure lifecycle model (deriveBinding /
    applyViewModeSelection), swaps the automerge source in place for ambient mode switches (same-view
    invariant), attaches the review extensions (own tracked changes, multi-author overlay, compare
    overlay, permanent change-bar gutter), filters overlay sources by the user's hiddenAuthors, and
    exposes `selectViewMode(ViewModeSelection)` as the single mode-change entry point.
```

```mdl
service ExtensionProvider
  desc: |
    Implements MarkdownCapabilities.ExtensionProvider (commentSync): syncs anchored comment threads
    with editor ranges, scopes visible comments to the active review branch (AnchoredTo.branch),
    tracks selection/comment overlap into CommentsState.toolbar, opens the comments companion on
    marker click, honours the review policy (`showComments`), prohibits inline comment creation on
    suggestion branches, and resolves anchors against the editor-bound Text.
```

```mdl
service ViewModeExtension
  desc: |
    Contributes the "Suggesting" entry to the markdown editor's view-mode dropdown
    (MarkdownCapabilities.ViewModeExtension, reviewMode 'suggesting'). No ReviewPlugin ⇒ no
    Suggesting entry.
```

```mdl
service ReviewRenderPolicy
  desc: |
    Maps a ReviewMode to its ReviewRenderConfig. The plugin contributes the GDocs-parity default;
    hosts override by contributing earlier in plugin order.
```

```mdl
service HistoryProvider
  desc: |
    Per-type opt-in to the generic History companion (checkpoints/branches timeline): `id` is the
    gating typename, `getTarget` resolves the versioned Text root. The plugin contributes the
    Markdown.Document provider; other object types opt in by contributing their own.
```

```mdl
service AgentRunner
  desc: |
    Capability that executes one agent turn for a thread + subject. Default implementation performs
    one LanguageModel.generateText call with edit tools registered per turn (editAnchoredRange,
    updateDocument). Stub implementations are used in storybook + tests.
  methods:
    run(input: { thread: Thread, subject: Obj.Any }) -> Effect<void>
```

## Operations

Comment-thread operations (keys `org.dxos.plugin.review.operation.<name>`):

```mdl
op Create
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.create
  desc: Create a (staged) comment thread anchored to a subject; seeds CommentsState.drafts.
  input: { subject: Obj.Any, anchor?: String, name?: String, branch?: String }

op AddMessage
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.addMessage
  desc: |
    Append a user message to a thread (promoting a staged draft to active). Evaluates the agent
    trigger gate and schedules RespondToThread when it passes.
  input: { subject: Obj.Any, anchor: AnchoredTo, sender: Actor, text: String }

op Delete
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.delete
  desc: Delete a thread + its anchor. Undoable via Restore.
  input: { anchor: AnchoredTo, subject: Obj.Any, thread?: Thread }
  output: { thread?: Thread, anchor?: AnchoredTo }

op Restore
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.restore
  desc: Inverse of Delete.
  input: { thread: Thread, anchor: AnchoredTo }

op DeleteMessage
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.deleteMessage
  desc: Delete a single message from a thread. Undoable via RestoreMessage.
  input: { anchor: AnchoredTo, subject: Obj.Any, messageId: String }
  output: { message?: Message, messageIndex?: Number }

op RestoreMessage
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.restoreMessage
  desc: Inverse of DeleteMessage.
  input: { anchor: AnchoredTo, message: Message, messageIndex: Number }

op SetResolved
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.setResolved
  desc: Set thread.status to active or resolved.
  input: { thread: Thread, resolved: boolean }
  requires: [Capability.Service]
  note: |
    Renamed from ToggleResolved, and not only a rename: the caller now states the status it wants
    rather than flipping whatever is current, so `resolved` is required.

op Select
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.select
  desc: Set the currently-selected thread (CommentsState.current); omit `current` to clear it.
  input: { current?: String }

op RespondToThread
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.respondToThread
  desc: Run one agent turn against a thread. Scheduled by AddMessage when the gate passes.
  input: { thread: Ref<Thread>, subject: Ref<Obj.Any> }

op SetAgentConfig
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.setAgentConfig
  desc: Mutate thread.agent. Undefined config means off.
  input: { thread: Ref<Thread>, config?: AgentConfig }

op CreateProposals
  key: org.dxos.operation.review.createProposals
  desc: |
    Materialise assistant-proposed document edits as NEW proposal-block comment threads, one per
    diff, each anchored to the document at the diff's cursor range.
  input: { doc: Ref<Markdown.Document>, diffs: String[] }
```

> Accept/reject of suggestions and proposals is NOT a plugin operation: every review surface (inline
> hover popover, ambient overlay, companion card) routes them through the durable
> `CollaborationOperation.AcceptChange` / `RejectChange` / `AcceptProposal` ops
> (`@dxos/app-toolkit`), which cherry-pick/revert the change against the author's branch and main
> (one hunk, cursor-anchored, undoable — invariant I-5). A branch whose last change is resolved
> archives itself (invariant I-6).

## Components

```mdl
component CommentsArticle
  desc: |
    Review companion surface (role 'article', linkedSegment 'comments') for a host object. Lists
    comment threads (AnchoredTo query + in-memory drafts, scoped to the branch under review) AND the
    suggestion review cards (Suggestions), with per-author visibility toggle chips. Tabs switch
    unresolved / all. The current change (viewAspect.suggestion) is shared with the editor: clicking
    a card reveals the change; clicking a change accents its card.
  props:
    attendableId?: String
    subject: Obj.Any

component ObjectHistory
  desc: |
    Generic History companion (gated by HistoryProvider): the git-graph Timeline of checkpoints,
    branches (with per-branch Tip nodes), forks and merges, plus Create revision / New branch /
    Merge / Discard actions. Selection drives the per-object VersioningView (shared with the editor
    binding). Nested branch-of-branch is guarded off (flat registry).
  props:
    subject: Obj.Any

component Suggestions
  desc: |
    Review companion for a document's `kind:'suggestion'` branches: SuggestionSources resolves live
    per-author content (+ fork-anchor base), buildSuggestionSources orders it, SuggestionAuthors
    renders the visibility toggle row, and SuggestionThread renders the (hidden-author-filtered)
    cards. Reactive: a card appears/updates as its author edits and disappears when
    accepted/rejected empties the branch.
  props:
    document?: VersionedObject
    base: String
    group?: GroupPolicy
    authorLabels?: Map<String, String>
    authorHues?: Map<String, String>
    selected?: { author: String, from: Number, to: Number }
    hiddenAuthors?: String[]
  emits:
    accept: { group: SuggestionGroup }
    reject: { group: SuggestionGroup }
    select: { group: SuggestionGroup }
    toggleAuthor: { author: String }

component SuggestionAuthors
  desc: |
    Per-author visibility toggles: one dx-tag chip per suggesting author in the author's hue, the
    eye icon inside the tag, hidden authors dimmed. Toggling filters that author out of every review
    surface (overlay, change bars, cards) for this user only — the branches are untouched.
  props:
    authors: { author: String, label: String, hue: Hue, hidden: Boolean }[]
  emits:
    toggle: { author: String }

component SuggestionThread
  desc: |
    Renders grouped changes as change-block tiles (before/after) with Accept/Reject, tinted with the
    author's hue. Built on @dxos/react-ui-thread Message.* with a ContentBlock.Change tile; renders
    nothing when empty. The card matching the current change is accented.
  props:
    base: String
    sources: SuggestionSource[]
    group?: GroupPolicy
    authorLabels?: Map<String, String>
    authorHues?: Map<String, String>
    selected?: { author: String, from: Number, to: Number }

component SuggestionSources
  desc: |
    Headless enumerator (render-prop + onResolved callback). Renders one invisible probe per active
    `kind:'suggestion'` branch, binds it, and reports the resolved ResolvedSuggestionBranch[] (with
    fork-anchor base) both synchronously and post-commit — backs the companion and the editor's
    ambient overlay.
  props:
    document: VersionedObject
    authorHues?: Map<String, String>
    onResolved?: (resolved: ResolvedSuggestionBranch[]) -> void

component VersionToolbar
  desc: |
    Editor banner for non-ambient selections: checkpoint / branch / fork context, the
    Base | Diff | Branch selector for a selected branch, and return-to-now. Ambient review has no
    banner — the view-mode dropdown is the only control.

component AgentToggle
  desc: |
    Per-thread radio popover hung off the thread header. Three states off / mention / auto; shows
    the resolved AgentIdentity.name as a read-only label. Routes through SetAgentConfig.
  props:
    value?: AgentConfig
    agentName: String
  emits:
    change: { config?: AgentConfig }
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Version-aware editor binding (the same-view invariant)

  req F-1.1: The plugin MUST contribute the editor binding via
    MarkdownCapabilities.EditorBindingHook; markdown itself carries no review vocabulary.

  req F-1.2: Ambient mode switches (Editing/Suggesting/Viewing) MUST NOT tear down the editor view:
    all ambient postures share one editor key, and entering/leaving Suggesting swaps the automerge
    source through a live compartment, preserving DOM, caret, focus and scroll (DESIGN §3.3).

  req F-1.3: Binding decisions MUST flow through the pure lifecycle model: deriveBinding (I-8) and
    applyViewModeSelection (I-9, one dropdown gesture writes the whole posture/view-mode pair).

  req F-1.4: Entering Suggesting MUST find-or-create the user's ONE suggestion branch
    (identity-stable, serialized) and reconcile a stale branch by folding main IN (I-2); typing in
    Suggesting MUST land on the branch and never on main (I-1).

  req F-1.5: After a view-mode dropdown selection the editor MUST regain focus with its caret
    intact; the editor MUST NOT steal focus on ambient/programmatic mode changes.

feat F-2: Suggestion rendering

  req F-2.1: A suggestion MUST render as the author's proposed text in the author's colour, replaced
    text struck through, a change bar, and a companion card. A pure block insertion carries its own
    change bar (the shared gutter never tints the host line's own text); whitespace-only newline
    runs render unstyled.

  req F-2.2: Each proposal MUST be diffed against the revision its author wrote on (the branch's
    fork anchor) and rebased into the viewing document's coordinates (I-3); a change already present
    in the document is not a suggestion (I-4).

  req F-2.3: Hunks MUST be minimal (an insert adjacent to identical text never strikes it) and
    markdown delimiter pairs (`**`…`**` etc.) MUST review — and apply — as ONE atomic change.

  req F-2.4: Text typed at a trailing suggestion's anchor MUST land after the proposal, never in
    front of it.

  req F-2.5: Toggling an author's visibility MUST remove that author's decorations, change bars and
    cards for this user only (source-level filter, session-local hiddenAuthors); the branches
    themselves are untouched.

feat F-3: Review workflow

  req F-3.1: Accept MUST fold exactly one change into main (cursor-anchored cherry-pick, undoable);
    Reject MUST revert it on the author's branch; both via CollaborationOperation, never a direct
    splice from a view (I-5).

  req F-3.2: When the last change on a suggestion branch is resolved the branch MUST archive itself
    (I-6).

  req F-3.3: The editor and the companion MUST share one current-change selection (viewAspect):
    click either side to reveal the other.

feat F-4: Version history

  req F-4.1: Checkpoint/fork/base views MUST render historical content read-only from detached
    snapshots (contentAt), never by binding the live doc to old heads (I-7).

  req F-4.2: The History companion (gated per-type by HistoryProvider) MUST expose checkpoints,
    branch tips, forks and merges on a git-graph timeline, with create/merge/discard actions;
    sub-branching is guarded off while the registry is flat.

feat F-5: Comment threads

  req F-5.1: The comment extension MUST create anchored threads from selections, keep AnchoredTo
    cursors in sync with edits, scope visibility to the active review branch, and honour the render
    policy's showComments.

  req F-5.2: Inline comment creation MUST be prohibited on suggestion branches (review of a
    suggestion happens on its card); comments live on main and draft branches.

  req F-5.3: Mutations MUST route through operations (never direct schema writes from views);
    Delete/DeleteMessage MUST be undoable.

feat F-6: Per-thread agent

  req F-6.1: Thread.agent gates AI involvement (absent/disabled = none); the trigger gate fires only
    on non-assistant messages of unresolved threads, in auto mode or on @mention of the resolved
    AgentIdentity.name; responses append as assistant messages; runner errors never lose the user's
    message.

feat F-7: Independence & testability

  req F-7.1: The plugin MUST NOT import other plugins' source; all cross-plugin wiring is via
    capabilities.

  req F-7.2: Core editing behaviour MUST be specified as shared scenarios (testing/scenarios.ts) run
    by BOTH the headless executor (real binding pipeline + real EditorView in a unit test) and the
    storybook play executor (full plugin stack), so the tiers cannot drift.
```

## Acceptance

Each DESIGN.md invariant names its enforcing test; the primary suites are:

```mdl
test T-1: Shared scenarios (both tiers)
  given: The scenario definitions in src/testing/scenarios.ts
  when: Run headless (src/testing/scenarios.test.tsx) and as storybook plays (Scenario*Test)
  then: |
    Editing goes to main with no review artifacts; suggesting goes to the own branch (tracked
    change, main untouched); deletion is a phantom; mode round-trips never double content, keep the
    suggestion a clean insert anchored before text typed at it, and hold editor focus after every
    dropdown selection; a multi-word bold wrap is ONE atomic suggestion; a suggested table is a
    clean block insertion; a table-cell edit stays inside the cell.

test T-2: Same-view swap
  given: The DocumentVersioning / SuggestingSwapTest play
  when: Suggesting is entered, typed into, and exited through the real dropdown
  then: One .cm-content DOM node and one EditorView across the whole round-trip; the caret survives;
    the edit lands on the branch as a tracked change and renders as the user's suggestion on exit.

test T-3: Lifecycle model
  given: The deriveBinding and applyViewModeSelection tables (review-lifecycle.test.ts)
  when: Every posture/selection/resolution combination is derived
  then: Subjects, keys, editability and loading match the tables; a stale readonly view mode cannot
    survive into Suggesting.

test T-4: Branch reconciliation (I-2)
  given: An existing suggestion branch with a stale anchor (main advanced), edited or not
  when: Suggesting is re-entered (find-or-create)
  then: The SAME branch id is returned; main's progress is folded in (CRDT); the author's edits
    survive; main's text never renders as the author's deletion.

test T-5: Diff-layer invariants (ui-editor review suite)
  given: diffHunks / pairMarkupHunks / rebaseHunks / cherryPickHunk unit tests
  then: Hunks are minimal; word replaces keep word granularity; delimiter pairs coalesce and apply
    atomically; a doc insertion at a trailing pure-insert anchor stays behind the proposal; applying
    every hunk reconstructs the proposal.

test T-6: Per-author visibility (F2.7)
  given: The AuthorVisibilityTest play (two seeded authors)
  when: One author is toggled off and back on in the companion
  then: That author's overlay and cards disappear and return; the other author is untouched; the
    branches survive.

test T-7: Comment/agent behaviour
  given: The comment operation and trigger-gate unit tests
  then: Auto mode responds once per user message; mention mode gates on @name; assistant messages
    and resolved threads never trigger; delete/restore round-trips; runner failures keep the user's
    message and emit `comments.agent.failed`.

test T-8: Walkthroughs
  given: TEST-PLAN.md F1–F6 against the DocumentVersioning / CommentsArticle stories
  then: The agent pre-runs every automatable step headlessly; a human pass confirms feel (latency,
    flicker, hover) that assertions cannot.
```

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Comment on a document, reply, and resolve
  desc: The comment-thread round-trip — anchor a thread on a document, reply, then resolve it.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-5.1, F-5.3, T-1, T-7]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - identity: an identity exists, its Actor used as the comment `sender`
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - doc: a Markdown document named "QA Review Doc" exists in the collection (created via
      plugin-markdown's [op:createDraft] and placed with `space.addObject`, per its own QA-1)
    - no comment thread anchored to "QA Review Doc" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this
      flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create a comment thread
      do: Select a word in the editor and click the comment icon in the selection popover.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.review.create { subject: $given.doc, anchor: "typo", name: "QA thread" }
      capture: created
      expect: a staged comment thread appears in the CommentsArticle companion, anchored to the
        selection
      assert: return !!$result.thread

    - name: Add a message
      do: Type "please fix this" and press Enter to send.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.review.addMessage { subject: $given.doc, anchor: $created.anchor, sender: $given.identity, text: "please fix this" }
      capture: added
      expect: the message appears in the thread, promoting it from staged to active
      assert: return $result.thread.messages.some((m) => m.id === $added.message?.id)

    - name: Resolve the thread
      do: Click the checkmark on the thread header.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.review.setResolved { thread: $added.thread, resolved: true }
      expect: the thread moves from the Unresolved tab to All, marked resolved
      assert: return $result.status === 'resolved'
  after:
    - name: Delete the thread
      do: Right-click the thread and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.review.delete { anchor: $created.anchor, subject: $given.doc, thread: $added.thread }
      expect: the thread no longer appears in the companion
```

